  "notes": "FORMS:\n{課|か} (impose, assign) + {金|きん} (money) → impose money/charges\n{課金|かきん}する (to charge, to bill; to make in-app purchases)\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- {課金|かきん}{制|せい} (fee-based system)\n- {従量|じゅうりょう}{課金|かきん} (usage-based billing)\n- {月額|げつがく}{課金|かきん} (monthly billing)\n- {無課金|むかきん} (free-to-play without paying)\n- {廃課金|はいかきん} (excessive in-app spending - slang)\n- {微課金|びかきん} (light spending - slang)\n\nMODERN USAGE:\nThe word has gained a new colloquial meaning in gaming culture, referring specifically to in-app purchases in mobile/online games. \"{課金|かきん}する\" can mean \"to pay real money in a game,\" often for gacha (loot box) systems or premium items.",
